# Installation Options:
- `--skip-clone`: Skip cloning repositories if they already exist
- `--skip-lTo install the GNAT LLVM toolchain (required for compiling Ada examples):
```bash
python3 scripts/install.py
```

## Installation Options:
- `--skip-clone`: Skip cloning repositories if they already exist
- `--skip-llvm`: Skip LLVM installation/build step
- `--build-gnatlib`: Attempt to build full runtime library (may fail)
- `--build-gnatlib-bc`: Build bitcode for GNAT runtime after main build

To build the LLVM BMC tool itself:
```bash
make
```


The script **`convert_examples.py`** compiles Ada files using GNAT LLVM and generates:

- LLVM IR (`.ll`)
- LLVM bitcode (`.bc`)
- Assembly (`.s`)

Output files are stored in:

```
conversions/
```

---

## Default Usage

Compile all examples from the default directory:

```bash
python3 convert_examples.py
```

Default input folder:

```
examples_1/
```

---

## Compile a Custom Directory

```bash
python3 convert_examples.py -d <directory>
```

Example:

```bash
python3 convert_examples.py -d examples
```

---

## Compile a Single Ada File

```bash
python3 convert_examples.py -f <file.adb>
```

Example:

```bash
python3 convert_examples.py -f examples/test.adb
```

